    "dislocate": {
      "word": "DISLOCATE",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To displace; to put out of its proper place. Especially, of a bone: To remove from its normal connections with a neighboring bone; to put out of joint; to move from its socket; to disjoint; as, to dislocate your bones. Shak. After some time the strata on all sides of the globe were dislocated. Woodward. And thus the archbishop's see, dislocated or out of joint for a time, was by the hands of his holiness set right again. Fuller.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dislocated. Montgomery.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        }
      ],
